# PC features (runtime games/pkp/pkp_play.cpp)
#   render resolution: the dynamic-resolution level table getters (level 30 = 1920x1080 is the docked full size) and their fallbacks,
#   and the per-frame copy of the render-size parameters (forces the full size while the game's dynamic resolution is off)
entryhook 0x7101129990
entryhook 0x71011299d0
entryhook 0x7101129980
entryhook 0x71011299c0
entryhook 0x710022d1e0
#   frame rate: the main loop's frame multiplier (dt * 60 clamped to [1, 3]); s0 = multiplier, s8 = dt at this join point
midhook 0x7100bfc4fc
#   frame rate: the main loop's 60 Hz Sync wait (0x710089def8): x22 = the frame period in ticks, right after the division
midhook 0x710089e27c
#   frame rate: its fixed-step frame time (1 / s0, s0 = 60.0), before the division
midhook 0x710089e398
#   frame rate: the area-transition scene sequence adds the frame multiplier to its timer, then skips its event while
#   timer != target. With fractional multipliers above 60 fps it can step past the target and leave the iris wipe closed
#   forever (#144). Skip only while timer < target instead, so equality or a crossing fires the event; no frame-rate cap.
patch 0x71004459bc 0x54000121 0x54000123
#   mouse camera: the follow camera's update (0x7100087840), right after it loaded the right stick's X (s0), x19 = the camera
midhook 0x7100087d30
