midhook 0x71017b6c98
#   keyboard prompts: the text layout (0x7101f90ca0) calling the inline tag handler ([obj+0x108]): w1 tag type, x2 args (UTF-16), x0 layout
midhook 0x7101f90fec
#   render resolution: the command context's SetViewport (0x71017b509c, x1 rect) and SetViewports (0x71017b5240, w1 count, x2 rects), after
#   their prologues: rects sized for 1920x1080 on render-size targets become the target size (viewport and the 2/w, -2/h screen constants)
midhook 0x71017b50ac
midhook 0x71017b5254
#   render resolution: the pass-state viewport recorder 0x71017c0420 (x0 = ctx + 0x10, w1 count, x2 rects; no screen constants of its own:
#   0x71017b3000 and friends derive 2/w, -2/h from what it records): rects sized for 1920x1080 on render-size targets become the target size
entryhook 0x71017c0420
#   render resolution (#44): the KTGL 2D render-target create 0x7101796810 (x0 device, w1 width, w2 height, w4 format; x30 the caller).
#   Call sites that pass a literal 1920x1080 (or a fraction of it) for a screen-relative target, among them the local-light buffer whose
#   light volumes texelFetch the render-size G-buffer at gl_FragCoord, get the render size from a per-call-site table (pkp_play.cpp).
#   (The terrain occlusion copy's mid hook 0x710073d824 is gone: the viewport recorder hook above already gives it the right source rect.)
entryhook 0x7101796810
